<% content_for :title, "Privacy — Potee" %>
<% content_for :auth_class, "guide" %>
<p class="back"><%= link_to "To the board", board_path %></p>
<h1>What data Potee keeps</h1>
<p class="lead">In short: what is stored, where it goes and how to ask for deletion.</p>

<h2 class="auth-subheading">Board</h2>
<p class="hint">Projects, milestones, their colours and order, the zoom and position of the board. A board
  without an account is recognised by a session cookie that lives for a year. A project you share can be
  seen and changed by anyone with the link.</p>

<h2 class="auth-subheading">Account</h2>
<p class="hint">Email, a password hash (the password itself is not stored), language, country for days off
  and board settings. Password reset letters go to your email. The token for AI agents is kept only as a
  SHA-256 hash, so it cannot be shown again.</p>

<h2 class="auth-subheading">Where you came from</h2>
<p class="hint">On the first visit Potee keeps the UTM tags of the link, the first page and the site you came
  from, without query parameters, and later the time of your last visit. This shows which publications bring
  people in.</p>

<h2 class="auth-subheading">Yandex Metrika</h2>
<p class="hint">Potee pages run a Yandex Metrika counter. It receives the page address without parameters
  (except UTM tags), the referring site and clicks on a few buttons such as «Get started». Webvisor, click
  map and form recording are off; password reset pages have no counter. Metrika sets its own cookies; you can
  <%= link_to "opt out as Yandex describes", "https://yandex.com/support/metrica/general/opt-out.html" %>.</p>

<h2 class="auth-subheading">Plan from text</h2>
<p class="hint">If you use the plan from text, your text goes to a language model through a private gateway:
  currently Anthropic Claude Haiku, with OpenAI GPT as a fallback, via OpenRouter. The request and the model
  answer are stored in the Potee database with your account.</p>

<h2 class="auth-subheading">Storage and deletion</h2>
<p class="hint">Data stays in the Potee database while the board or account exists. Anonymous boards that
  have not been opened for a long time may be deleted. To delete your account and data, write to
  <%= mail_to "danil@pismenny.ru" %> from the account email.</p>
